  faqs: [
    { question: "Does Kozhikode have any school that actually teaches IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Not currently, as far as can be confirmed: no school in Kozhikode appears as an authorised IB World School or a Cambridge International centre. Most local IB or IGCSE students are either returning from a curriculum studied abroad, enrolled in a recognised online school, or preparing to join a Diploma school outside Kerala. IB Gram works with all three situations." },
    { question: "How do I get my child matched with a tutor here?", answer: "Send us the programme or board, subject, level and exam series, and we shortlist tutors who have actually taught that course. Since Kozhikode has no local school to draw from, the match runs entirely on syllabus fit, checked afterward against your family's evening hours. A free trial runs online before anything is decided." },
    { question: "My child studied abroad and we've moved back to Kozhikode. Can you help?", answer: "Yes, and this is one of the most common situations we see from Kozhikode, given the city's long history of Gulf migration. We match a tutor to the exact curriculum and level your child was studying, British, American or otherwise, so the transition continues rather than restarts from scratch." },
    { question: "Will a tutor visit our home in Kozhikode?", answer: "No. That kind of visit happens only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. In Kozhikode, every lesson runs live online, one to one, over video with a shared whiteboard, which is genuine private tuition delivered at home rather than a promise that someone arrives at your door." },
    { question: "Do you cover both Cambridge and Edexcel IGCSE?", answer: "Yes. Cambridge students are matched down to the exact code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620 for instance, and Edexcel students by specification and Foundation or Higher tier, using each board's own past papers and mark schemes throughout." },
    { question: "What does a tutor cost for a Kozhikode family?", answer: "Programme, level, subject, session length and the tutor's own recent experience with the syllabus all feed into the number, which gets locked in for your match before the trial, never changed afterward. Diploma HL work sits above MYP or IGCSE Core pricing. Nothing is added for travel, since every session is online, and no contract ties a family in past the point it wants to stop." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial before we commit to anything?", answer: "Every single match starts this way, no exceptions. Your child sits through a lesson on their own actual syllabus content, at zero cost and with no strings attached. What follows the trial is a short plan for month one, and the decision to proceed, tweak the plan, or ask for a different tutor entirely is entirely yours from there." },
    { question: "Can a tutor write parts of my child's Internal Assessment?", answer: "Never. What is allowed is help narrowing down a research question, a plain explanation of what each grading criterion is actually looking for, a sanity check on a data-collection approach, and candid feedback on a draft. The line stops exactly where the assessed work itself begins, regardless of how the request is phrased." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects does IB Gram cover for Kozhikode students?", answer: "Most demand clusters around a fairly predictable set: both Maths routes at HL and SL, the three sciences, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, with Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay support offered on top of whichever subject a student is already taking." },
    { question: "What about younger students, not just the Diploma?", answer: "MYP and PYP both get the same attention as the Diploma. Younger MYP students typically need help writing to criteria in the sciences and in Language and Literature, plus keeping a Personal Project journal on track. PYP tutoring centres on reading, writing and number confidence, building toward the research skills an eventual Exhibition will demand." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring actually reliable with no local specialist to compare it to?", answer: "Reliability is not really the question here; availability is. With no confirmed IB or Cambridge school anywhere in Kozhikode, an online specialist is not a substitute for a local one, it is simply where the actual expertise lives. Screen-sharing, live past papers and recorded explanations do almost everything an in-room session would." },
    { question: "How does IB Gram check a tutor before we meet them?", answer: "Qualifications get checked, so does how recently and how well a tutor has taught that specific subject and level, and so does their track record on assessment criteria, all before any family is introduced. A generalist rarely makes the cut here, given how little local competition Kozhikode's own thin base creates. After that, the trial class is where you form your own judgement." },
    { question: "When is the right time to start tutoring?", answer: "Right when the course itself begins works best, Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma, since that timing leaves room to patch gaps before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades all start arriving in quick succession. A late start in the final year is not wasted either, provided the sessions stay narrowly aimed at past papers and the topics carrying the most marks." },
    { question: "We're considering switching our child from CBSE to IGCSE. What actually changes?", answer: "Content is rarely the obstacle; exam technique is. A student needs direct teaching in what words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' actually require, plus an entirely new set of habits around planning coursework or an IA, none of which CBSE really demands. A summer holiday spent on exactly this before the switch pays off." },
    { question: "Can sessions fit around Kozhikode's monsoon and festival calendar?", answer: "That is built into the planning by default. Evening slots shift around the worst of the June-September monsoon, Onam is treated as a genuine school-calendar pause rather than an inconvenience, and Eid gets the same respect where it matters to a family. Squeezing in an extra weekly slot before an exam series is simple since nothing depends on travel." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected to any school or exam board?", answer: "It is not, anywhere, including in Kozhikode. There is no relationship with the International Baccalaureate Organization, with Cambridge Assessment International Education, with Pearson Edexcel, or with any school this page mentions. Every tutor works from that school's own calendar and whatever syllabus the relevant board has actually published." },
  ],

